\import{discrete-macros}

\title{\False}
\date{2026-02-09T14:04:58Z}
\tag{discrete}

\p{There is no way to prove \False.}

\transclude{005I}

\p{If you know \False, then you know \em{anything you want}.  (This principle is sometimes called \em{ex falso quodlibet}, or just \em{ex falso} for short.  This is Latin for "from false, whatever you want".)}
